            <ArticleTitle>Antiphospholipid antibodies and splenic thrombosis in a patient with idiopathic myelofibrosis (antiphospholipid antibodies and thrombosis).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>516-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of idiopathic myelofibrosis and hepatosplenic myeloid metaplasia associated with antiphospholipids antibodies is described. The patient developed a lethal complete splenic vein thrombosis in spite of an intravenously heparin treatment had been started soon after a clinical pattern of &quot;acute abdomen&quot;.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
